column2:
There is a young man who [came he]re —
149	in all the land his st[rength is] the strongest;
150	his might is as hard as a lump of the sky-rock of Anu.
151	He roams over the hills all the time;
152	all the time with the herd I see him grazing;
153	all the time his feet are planted at the lip of the watering-place.
154	I am afraid; I dare not go near [h]im.
155	He fills in the pits I my[self] dig;
156	he tears out the traps [I spr]ead;
157	he frees from my hands the herds, the beas[ts of] the steppe;
158	he will not let me work the steppe.

The stars of the sky came out for you;
260	[li]ke a lump of the sky-rock of Anu one kept falling down at you.
261	You lifted it: it was too strong for you;
262	you heaved at it: you could not shift it;
263	you lifted it and set it down at my feet,
264	and I — I made it equal with y[ou;]
265	you loved it like a wife, bending murmuring over it:
266	there will come to you a strong one, a companion, the rescuer of a friend.
267	In all the land his strength is the strongest;
268	his might is as hard as a lump of the sky-rock of Anu.
269	You will love him like a wife, bending murmuring over him,
270	and he, the strong one, will time and again save you.

Mother, by the mouth of Enlil the great counsellor let it fall to me!
294	A friend, a counsellor, let me get;
295	[let me g]et a friend, a counsellor!
